  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.96,
      "end_seconds": 6.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Right, hello, sorry about the delay, do sit. What's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.61,
      "end_seconds": 14.1,
      "duration_seconds": 6.49,
      "text": "Hmm, so the thing is, I've got a swollen red eyelid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 15.46,
      "end_seconds": 24.87,
      "duration_seconds": 9.41,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temp 38.7 degrees, pulse is 91 beats a minute, saturation 95 percent, pressure 123 over 71."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.67,
      "end_seconds": 31.37,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.03,
      "end_seconds": 41.24,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.25,
      "end_seconds": 47.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "It's, It's been going on for about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.81,
      "end_seconds": 53.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Right, is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.45,
      "end_seconds": 57.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "It happens every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.58,
      "end_seconds": 64.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Any pain on moving the eye as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.71,
      "end_seconds": 70.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Yeah, I've had that since this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.39,
      "end_seconds": 81.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "Have you had a swollen red eyelid before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.34,
      "end_seconds": 96.7,
      "duration_seconds": 9.36,
      "text": "Um, yes, something like this happened about six months ago, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.92,
      "end_seconds": 104.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Have you had any blurred vision or sinus infection?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.48,
      "end_seconds": 110.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Right, uh, nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.44,
      "end_seconds": 113.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Did you notice any recent injury?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.53,
      "end_seconds": 116.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "No, no recent injury."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.68,
      "end_seconds": 121.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "So, is your urine normal, no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.39,
      "end_seconds": 125.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Actually, no, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.78,
      "end_seconds": 134.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.13,
      "end_seconds": 138.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "No, uh, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.22,
      "end_seconds": 156.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.39,
      "end_seconds": 163.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "Febuxostat. I take it 80 milligrams, maybe, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.78,
      "end_seconds": 170.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.04,
      "end_seconds": 175.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Ah, not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.31,
      "end_seconds": 180.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.55,
      "end_seconds": 194.08,
      "duration_seconds": 12.53,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day. I grab fast food at lunch most days. Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.21,
      "end_seconds": 197.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.72,
      "end_seconds": 203.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "Yeah, I've had gout for about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.48,
      "end_seconds": 213.89,
      "duration_seconds": 8.41,
      "text": "Right, so gout is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.86,
      "end_seconds": 221.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "Hmm, no, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.61,
      "end_seconds": 227.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.54,
      "end_seconds": 232.24,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.46,
      "end_seconds": 234.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.51,
      "end_seconds": 259.86,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "The eyelid is swollen shut, the eye is bulging and the movements are painful and limited."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.58,
      "end_seconds": 273.16,
      "duration_seconds": 10.58,
      "text": "Okay, you can relax now. Okay, thinking it through, this is probably orbital cellulitis. I'd also keep periorbital cellulitis in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.01,
      "end_seconds": 276.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.16,
      "end_seconds": 286.38,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now orbital cellulitis is my leading thought, not anything worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.05,
      "end_seconds": 328.23,
      "duration_seconds": 30.18,
      "text": "I'll request blood tests, it'll help with orbital cellulitis. I want an urgent CT scan done, that's for orbital cellulitis. You need admission today for intravenous antibiotics. Let's get you seen by the eye team, I'll arrange the letter. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Let's review you straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.31,
      "end_seconds": 332.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Good, I'll return then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.19,
      "end_seconds": 339.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.38,
      "end_seconds": 344.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "That's clear, you know, thanks."
    }
  ]
